      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal|Guarded Write Journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal (either the file\u0027s previous content, or a record that it didn\u0027t exist)\n- If an agent run fails (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal rolls back every write in reverse order\n- This provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log, kept in process memory for the duration of a run\n- The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback functionality since it has no write capability",
